course: dictionary
lesson: 13498
title: Author and illustrator
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An illustrator is a person who draws or paints the pictures for books, magazines, posters or websites. Look at the words around the word to find its meaning. «The illustrator drew a fox with a bright red scarf.» Who drew the fox? The illustrator did, so the illustrator makes the pictures.
explain: Many books have two makers. «The author wrote the story, and the illustrator painted every page.» The author writes the words, and the illustrator makes the pictures. On many covers you will see the two names together: author and illustrator.
explain: Use the swap check. «The illustrator painted the poster for the school fair.» Swap in the meaning: "the person who draws pictures painted the poster for the school fair." It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: An illustrator is a person who draws or paints pictures.
fact: Illustrators make pictures for books, magazines, posters and websites.
fact: In a book, the author writes the words and the illustrator draws the pictures.
fact: A children's book illustrator draws the pictures in books for young readers.
exercise: «The illustrator drew a fox with a bright red scarf.» Who draws pictures like this? | A person who reads the story aloud | A person who writes the words of a story | A person who sells books in a shop | *A person who draws or paints pictures
exercise: What does an illustrator make? | Music for a film | Words for the story | *Pictures for books, posters or websites | Maps of the town
exercise: «The author wrote the story, and the illustrator painted every page.» Find and copy the one word that names the person who draws the pictures. | painted | story | author | *illustrator
test: The cover says «Words by Sam Reid, pictures by Priya Nair.» Who is the illustrator? | Cover | Words | Sam Reid | *Priya Nair
test: What do we call a book's writer and picture-maker when we name them together? | editor and printer | teacher and pupil | reader and librarian | *author and illustrator
exam: «The illustrator's bright pictures made the poster for the summer fair.» What job does an illustrator do? | Organises the fair | Writes the poster's words only | Sells tickets at the door | *Draws or paints pictures for posters
